CloudBurrow patch 44 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1466). Applies after patch 0041.

The gaps: BigQuery keeps the contents a CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE
replaces, "the data that is replaced or removed can be recovered through
the time travel window" (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/time-travel),
but patch 0036 started the table's change table over, so FOR SYSTEM_TIME
AS OF a time before the replace, APPENDS and CHANGES had nothing to read.
And the engine's clock (CURRENT_TIMESTAMP() and the change times) is the
system's, while CloudBurrow's front advances its own clock in tests: a
time travel window or a CHANGES range measured by one clock and read by
the other.

The patch keeps the change table of the table a CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE
replaces and carries it into the new one: its changes, with the values
of each column the new table has of the same name and type, its START
row in place of the new one, and a DELETE, at the time of the replace,
of each row the replaced table still had (as a WRITE_TRUNCATE records the
rows it replaces), the old rows' rowids moved below every rowid. And it
gives the engine a clock offset, googlesqlite.SetClockOffset, which
CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(), CURRENT_DATE(), CURRENT_DATETIME(), CURRENT_TIME()
and the change times read; bigquery-emulator patch 0034 serves it to the
front. change_history_replace_test.go fails without the patch and passes
with it.

